IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `dg-core`
IMPORT `dg11-s391-fees`

-- Delaware General Corporation Law, 8 Del. C. ch. 1 -- piece dg11, Subchapter XVII:
-- section 390, "Transfer, domestication or continuance of domestic corporations".
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively. It takes nobody's point of view; the seat layer dg11-seat.l4 asks these rules as questions.
--
-- The source is the plain-text rendering de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt (not the official text). `-- src:N | ...` is line N of it.
--
-- The section lets a corporation of this State move out: it TRANSFERS to a foreign jurisdiction (its existence as a Delaware corporation ceases),
-- or DOMESTICATES or CONTINUES there while ELECTING to keep its Delaware existence too. The two certificates are the certificate of transfer
-- (existence ceases) and the certificate of transfer and domestic continuance (existence continues).
--
-- OUT OF RANGE (taken as plain inputs, never recomputed):
--   * § 103 (piece dg1): that an instrument was executed in accordance with § 103, and the time at which it becomes effective.
--   * § 391 (this piece): the fee for the certificate; see dg11-s391-fees.l4 (`s 391(a)(25)`).
--   * the Attorney General's side of the notice in subsection (i) is an official; no seat.
--   * the nonstock reading of "stockholders" and "board of directors" (§ 114(a), piece dg1) is taken as the Law's reading: a nonstock corporation's
--     governing body does what the board does; its members do what the stockholders do (subsection (i) says so itself).
-- Dates are data: the only absolute date a rule here depends on is 1 August 2023 (subsection (k)).

§ `Section 390(a) - who may move out, and the definitions`

-- src:2004 | (a) Upon compliance with the provisions of this section, any corporation existing under the laws of this State may transfer to or domesticate or continue in any foreign jurisdiction and, in connection therewith, may elect to continue its existence as a corporation of this State. As used in this section, the term:
-- src:2005 | (1) “Foreign jurisdiction” means any foreign country, or other foreign jurisdiction (other than the United States, any state, the District of Columbia, or any possession or territory of the United States); and
-- Gloss: the core's `Where an entity is formed` has three leaves; only `a foreign jurisdiction outside the United States` is a "foreign jurisdiction" in this section.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 390(a)(1) (src:2005)
GIVEN place IS A `Where an entity is formed`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 390(a)(1) the place is a foreign jurisdiction` place MEANS
    place EQUALS `a foreign jurisdiction outside the United States`

-- src:2006 | (2) “Resulting entity” means the entity formed, incorporated, created or otherwise coming into being as a consequence of the transfer of the corporation to, or its domestication or continuance in, a foreign jurisdiction pursuant to this section.
-- Gloss: the resulting entity is the entity that comes into being in the foreign jurisdiction as a consequence of the transfer, domestication or continuance. It is a status of an entity, so it is a fact the caller states
-- wherever a rule below speaks of it (an entity is the resulting entity if it came into being in that way).
@ref 8 Del. C. § 390(a)(2) (src:2006)
GIVEN `the entity was formed, incorporated, created or otherwise came into being as a consequence of the transfer of the corporation to, or its domestication or continuance in, a foreign jurisdiction pursuant to this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 390(a)(2) the entity is the resulting entity` `the entity was formed, incorporated, created or otherwise came into being as a consequence of the transfer of the corporation to, or its domestication or continuance in, a foreign jurisdiction pursuant to this section` MEANS
    `the entity was formed, incorporated, created or otherwise came into being as a consequence of the transfer of the corporation to, or its domestication or continuance in, a foreign jurisdiction pursuant to this section`

-- Gloss: "Upon compliance with the provisions of this section": the five steps the section requires, each decided by a rule below, are inputs here.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 390(a) (src:2004)
GIVEN `the corporation exists under the laws of this State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the jurisdiction` IS A `Where an entity is formed`
      `the board has adopted the resolution and submitted it to the stockholders as subsection (b) requires` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the stockholders have approved, or no vote of the stockholders is necessary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate required by subsection (b) has been filed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 390(a) the corporation may transfer to, or domesticate or continue in, the foreign jurisdiction` `the corporation exists under the laws of this State` `the jurisdiction` `the board has adopted the resolution and submitted it to the stockholders as subsection (b) requires` `the stockholders have approved, or no vote of the stockholders is necessary` `the certificate required by subsection (b) has been filed` MEANS
        `the corporation exists under the laws of this State`
    AND `s 390(a)(1) the place is a foreign jurisdiction` `the jurisdiction`
    AND `the board has adopted the resolution and submitted it to the stockholders as subsection (b) requires`
    AND `the stockholders have approved, or no vote of the stockholders is necessary`
    AND `the certificate required by subsection (b) has been filed`

-- src:2004 | any corporation existing under the laws of this State may transfer to or domesticate or continue in any foreign jurisdiction and, in connection therewith, may elect to continue its existence as a corporation of this State.
-- The election: a corporation that moves out may keep its existence as a corporation of this State. Which of the two certificates it files shows the election (subsection (b)).
@ref 8 Del. C. § 390(a) (src:2004)
DECLARE `s 390(b) Certificate to be filed with the Secretary of State` IS ONE OF
    `a certificate of transfer`
    `a certificate of transfer and domestic continuance`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 390(a) (src:2004); § 390(b) (src:2007)
GIVEN `the corporation elects to continue its existence as a corporation of this State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 390(b) Certificate to be filed with the Secretary of State`
`s 390(b) the certificate that the corporation files` `the corporation elects to continue its existence as a corporation of this State` MEANS
    IF   `the corporation elects to continue its existence as a corporation of this State`
    THEN `a certificate of transfer and domestic continuance`
    ELSE `a certificate of transfer`

§ `Section 390(b) - the resolution, the meeting, the vote and the certificate`

-- src:2007 | (b) The board of directors of the corporation which desires to transfer to or domesticate or continue in a foreign jurisdiction shall adopt a resolution approving such transfer, domestication or continuance specifying the foreign jurisdiction to which the corporation shall be transferred or in which the corporation shall be domesticated or continued and, if applicable, that in connection with such transfer, domestication or continuance the corporation’s existence as a corporation of this State is to continue and recommending the approval of such transfer or domestication or continuance by the stockholders of the corporation.
-- src:2007 | If a plan of transfer, domestication or continuance is to be adopted in accordance with subsection (j) of this section, such plan shall be approved together with the resolution approving the transfer, domestication or continuance.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 390(b) (src:2007)
DECLARE `s 390(b) Resolution of the board of directors` HAS
    `resolution approving the transfer, domestication or continuance adopted by the board of directors`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `resolution specifies the foreign jurisdiction`                                                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `resolution states that the corporation's existence as a corporation of this State is to continue`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `resolution recommends approval by the stockholders`                                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `plan of transfer, domestication or continuance approved together with the resolution`                    IS A BOOLEAN

-- Gloss: the statement that the Delaware existence is to continue is needed "if applicable" (when the corporation elects to continue); the plan is approved together with the resolution only
-- "if a plan ... is to be adopted".
@ref 8 Del. C. § 390(b) (src:2007)
GIVEN resolution IS A `s 390(b) Resolution of the board of directors`
      `the corporation elects to continue its existence as a corporation of this State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a plan of transfer, domestication or continuance is to be adopted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 390(b) the board has adopted the resolution as subsection (b) requires` resolution `the corporation elects to continue its existence as a corporation of this State` `a plan of transfer, domestication or continuance is to be adopted` MEANS
        resolution's `resolution approving the transfer, domestication or continuance adopted by the board of directors`
    AND resolution's `resolution specifies the foreign jurisdiction`
    AND ((NOT `the corporation elects to continue its existence as a corporation of this State`) OR resolution's `resolution states that the corporation's existence as a corporation of this State is to continue`)
    AND resolution's `resolution recommends approval by the stockholders`
    AND ((NOT `a plan of transfer, domestication or continuance is to be adopted`) OR resolution's `plan of transfer, domestication or continuance approved together with the resolution`)

-- src:2007 | Such resolution shall be submitted to the stockholders of the corporation at an annual or special meeting.
-- src:2007 | Due notice of the time, place and purpose of the meeting shall be given to each holder of stock, whether voting or nonvoting, of the corporation at the address of the stockholder as it appears on the records of the corporation, at least 20 days prior to the date of the meeting.
-- Gloss: the notice goes to EVERY holder of stock, voting or not, at the address on the corporation's records, and states the time, place and purpose of the meeting. "At least 20 days prior to the date of the meeting":
-- notice given exactly 20 days before the meeting is in time (Fork register F-390-1).
@ref 8 Del. C. § 390(b) (src:2007)
GIVETH A Period
`s 390(b) the least notice of the meeting` MEANS `period in days` 20

@ref 8 Del. C. § 390(b) (src:2007)
DECLARE `s 390(b) Notice of the meeting of the stockholders` HAS
    `meeting at which the resolution is submitted is an annual or special meeting`                                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `notice states the time, place and purpose of the meeting`                                                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `notice is given to each holder of stock, whether voting or nonvoting, at the address on the corporation's records`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `date on which the notice was given`                                                                                        IS A DATE
    `date of the meeting`                                                                                                       IS A DATE

@ref 8 Del. C. § 390(b) (src:2007)
GIVEN notice IS A `s 390(b) Notice of the meeting of the stockholders`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 390(b) the notice of the meeting was given as required` notice MEANS
        notice's `meeting at which the resolution is submitted is an annual or special meeting`
    AND notice's `notice states the time, place and purpose of the meeting`
    AND notice's `notice is given to each holder of stock, whether voting or nonvoting, at the address on the corporation's records`
    AND (notice's `date on which the notice was given` AT MOST (`the date` `s 390(b) the least notice of the meeting` `before` (notice's `date of the meeting`)))

-- src:2007 | At the meeting, the resolution shall be considered and a vote taken for its adoption or rejection.
-- src:2007 | If a majority of the outstanding shares of stock of the corporation, entitled to vote thereon shall be voted for the adoption of the resolution (provided that, if the corporation is transferring, domesticating or continuing as a partnership having 1 or more general partners, then, in addition to the foregoing approval, authorization of the transfer, domestication or continuance shall require approval of each stockholder of the corporation who will become a general partner of such partnership as a result of the transfer, domestication or continuance), the corporation shall file with the Secretary of State a certificate of transfer if its existence as a corporation of this State is to cease or a certificate of transfer and domestic continuance if its existence as a corporation of this State is to continue, executed in accordance with § 103 of this title, which certifies:
-- Gloss: the vote is "a majority of the outstanding shares of stock ... entitled to vote thereon" (more than half; the core's `a majority of` the outstanding stock entitled to vote). Counts are votes (§ 212(a), Instruction 9 of the keel).
-- Where the corporation moves as a partnership with 1 or more general partners, EACH stockholder who will become a general partner must also approve (the count approving must equal the count who will become general partners).
-- Counts that cannot be a vote are NOTHING (not covered), never FALSE.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 390(b) (src:2007)
GIVEN `the votes in favor of adopting the resolution` IS A NUMBER
      `the outstanding stock entitled to vote thereon, in votes` IS A NUMBER
      `the corporation is transferring, domesticating or continuing as a partnership having 1 or more general partners` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of stockholders who will become a general partner as a result` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of those stockholders who approve` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 390(b) the stockholders have adopted the resolution` `the votes in favor of adopting the resolution` `the outstanding stock entitled to vote thereon, in votes` `the corporation is transferring, domesticating or continuing as a partnership having 1 or more general partners` `the number of stockholders who will become a general partner as a result` `the number of those stockholders who approve` MEANS
    IF   (`the number of stockholders who will become a general partner as a result` AT LEAST 0)
         AND (`the number of those stockholders who approve` AT LEAST 0)
         AND (`the number of those stockholders who approve` AT MOST `the number of stockholders who will become a general partner as a result`)
    THEN CONSIDER `the vote carries` (`a majority of` `the outstanding stock entitled to vote`) `the votes in favor of adopting the resolution` `the outstanding stock entitled to vote thereon, in votes`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
         WHEN JUST carried THEN JUST (carried AND ((NOT `the corporation is transferring, domesticating or continuing as a partnership having 1 or more general partners`) OR (`the number of those stockholders who approve` EQUALS `the number of stockholders who will become a general partner as a result`)))
    ELSE NOTHING

-- The proviso seen from one stockholder's side: if the corporation is moving as a partnership with 1 or more general partners, the authorization "shall require approval of each stockholder of the corporation who will become
-- a general partner" -- so a stockholder who will become a general partner has a veto, and one who will not has none.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 390(b) (src:2007)
GIVEN `the corporation is transferring, domesticating or continuing as a partnership having 1 or more general partners` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the stockholder will become a general partner of the partnership as a result` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 390(b) the approval of the stockholder is required for the authorization, in addition to the vote` `the corporation is transferring, domesticating or continuing as a partnership having 1 or more general partners` `the stockholder will become a general partner of the partnership as a result` MEANS
    `the corporation is transferring, domesticating or continuing as a partnership having 1 or more general partners` AND `the stockholder will become a general partner of the partnership as a result`

-- src:2008 | (1) The name of the corporation, and if it has been changed, the name under which it was originally incorporated.
-- src:2009 | (2) The date of filing of its original certificate of incorporation with the Secretary of State.
-- src:2010 | (3) The foreign jurisdiction to which the corporation shall be transferred or in which it shall be domesticated or continued and the name of the resulting entity.
-- src:2011 | (4) That the transfer, domestication or continuance of the corporation has been approved in accordance with the provisions of this section.
-- src:2012 | (5) In the case of a certificate of transfer, (i) that the existence of the corporation as a corporation of this State shall cease when the certificate of transfer becomes effective, and (ii) the agreement of the corporation that it may be served with process in this State in any proceeding for enforcement of any obligation of the corporation arising while it was a corporation of this State which shall also irrevocably appoint the Secretary of State as its agent to accept service of process in any such proceeding and specify the address (which may not be that of the corporation’s registered agent without the written consent of the corporation’s registered agent, such consent to be filed along with the certificate of transfer) to which a copy of such process shall be mailed by the Secretary of State. …
-- src:2013 | (6) In the case of a certificate of transfer and domestic continuance, that the corporation will continue to exist as a corporation of this State after the certificate of transfer and domestic continuance becomes effective.
-- src:2014 | (7) If a plan of transfer, domestication or continuance is adopted in accordance with subsection (j) of this section, that all provisions of the plan of transfer, domestication or continuance shall be approved in accordance with this section.
-- Gloss: what the certificate must certify: (1) to (4) always; (5) in a certificate of transfer only; (6) in a certificate of transfer and domestic continuance only; (7) only if a plan is adopted.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 390(b)(1) to (7) (src:2008-2014)
DECLARE `s 390(b) What the certificate certifies` HAS
    `name of the corporation and, if it has been changed, the name under which it was originally incorporated`                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `date of filing of its original certificate of incorporation with the Secretary of State`                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `foreign jurisdiction and the name of the resulting entity`                                                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `that the transfer, domestication or continuance has been approved in accordance with this section`                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `that the existence of the corporation as a corporation of this State shall cease when the certificate of transfer becomes effective` IS A BOOLEAN
    `agreement that the corporation may be served with process in this State, irrevocably appointing the Secretary of State as its agent and specifying an address` IS A BOOLEAN
    `that the corporation will continue to exist as a corporation of this State after the certificate becomes effective`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `that all provisions of the plan shall be approved in accordance with this section`                                             IS A BOOLEAN

@ref 8 Del. C. § 390(b)(1) to (7) (src:2008-2014)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 390(b) Certificate to be filed with the Secretary of State`
      certifies IS A `s 390(b) What the certificate certifies`
      `a plan of transfer, domestication or continuance is adopted in accordance with subsection (j)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 390(b) the certificate certifies everything that subsection (b) requires` kind certifies `a plan of transfer, domestication or continuance is adopted in accordance with subsection (j)` MEANS
        certifies's `name of the corporation and, if it has been changed, the name under which it was originally incorporated`
    AND certifies's `date of filing of its original certificate of incorporation with the Secretary of State`
    AND certifies's `foreign jurisdiction and the name of the resulting entity`
    AND certifies's `that the transfer, domestication or continuance has been approved in accordance with this section`
    AND ((NOT (kind EQUALS `a certificate of transfer`))
         OR (    certifies's `that the existence of the corporation as a corporation of this State shall cease when the certificate of transfer becomes effective`
             AND certifies's `agreement that the corporation may be served with process in this State, irrevocably appointing the Secretary of State as its agent and specifying an address`))
    AND ((NOT (kind EQUALS `a certificate of transfer and domestic continuance`))
         OR certifies's `that the corporation will continue to exist as a corporation of this State after the certificate becomes effective`)
    AND ((NOT `a plan of transfer, domestication or continuance is adopted in accordance with subsection (j)`)
         OR certifies's `that all provisions of the plan shall be approved in accordance with this section`)

-- Gloss: the address for the mailing of a copy of process "may not be that of the corporation's registered agent without the written consent of the corporation's registered agent, such consent to be filed along with the certificate of transfer".
@ref 8 Del. C. § 390(b) (src:2012)
GIVEN `the address specified is that of the corporation's registered agent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the written consent of the registered agent is filed along with the certificate of transfer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 390(b)(5) the address specified for the mailing of a copy of process is permitted` `the address specified is that of the corporation's registered agent` `the written consent of the registered agent is filed along with the certificate of transfer` MEANS
    (NOT `the address specified is that of the corporation's registered agent`) OR `the written consent of the registered agent is filed along with the certificate of transfer`

-- src:2012 | Process may be served upon the Secretary of State under this subsection by means of electronic transmission but only as prescribed by the Secretary of State. …
-- out of range: the manner prescribed by the Secretary of State (an instrument of the Secretary of State, not among the inputs): a BOOLEAN fact.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 390(b)(5) (src:2012)
GIVEN `the service by electronic transmission is made as prescribed by the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 390(b)(5) process may be served upon the Secretary of State by electronic transmission` `the service by electronic transmission is made as prescribed by the Secretary of State` MEANS
    `the service by electronic transmission is made as prescribed by the Secretary of State`

-- src:2012 | In the event of service upon the Secretary of State in accordance with this subsection, the Secretary of State shall forthwith notify such corporation that has transferred out of the State of Delaware by letter, directed to such corporation that has transferred out of the State of Delaware at the address so specified, unless such corporation shall have designated in writing to the Secretary of State a different address for such purpose, in which case it shall be mailed to the last address designated. …
-- Gloss: the Secretary of State's letter goes to the address specified in the certificate, unless the corporation has designated a different address in writing, in which case to the LAST address designated.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 390(b)(5) (src:2012)
GIVEN `the address specified in the certificate of transfer` IS A STRING
      `the last different address that the corporation designated in writing to the Secretary of State, if any` IS A MAYBE STRING
GIVETH A STRING
`s 390(b)(5) the address to which the Secretary of State mails the letter notifying the corporation of the service` `the address specified in the certificate of transfer` `the last different address that the corporation designated in writing to the Secretary of State, if any` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the last different address that the corporation designated in writing to the Secretary of State, if any`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the address specified in the certificate of transfer`
    WHEN JUST designated THEN designated

-- src:2012 | Such letter shall be sent by a mail or courier service that includes a record of mailing or deposit with the courier and a record of delivery evidenced by the signature of the recipient. Such letter shall enclose a copy of the process and any other papers served on the Secretary of State pursuant to this subsection. …
-- Gloss: the letter is sent by a mail or courier service that keeps a record of mailing or deposit with the courier AND a record of delivery evidenced by the signature of the recipient, and encloses a copy of the process and any other papers served.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 390(b)(5) (src:2012)
GIVEN `it is sent by a mail or courier service that includes a record of mailing or deposit with the courier` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it includes a record of delivery evidenced by the signature of the recipient` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it encloses a copy of the process and any other papers served on the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 390(b)(5) the letter notifying the corporation of the service is sent as required` `it is sent by a mail or courier service that includes a record of mailing or deposit with the courier` `it includes a record of delivery evidenced by the signature of the recipient` `it encloses a copy of the process and any other papers served on the Secretary of State` MEANS
        `it is sent by a mail or courier service that includes a record of mailing or deposit with the courier`
    AND `it includes a record of delivery evidenced by the signature of the recipient`
    AND `it encloses a copy of the process and any other papers served on the Secretary of State`

-- src:2012 | It shall be the duty of the plaintiff in the event of such service to serve process and any other papers in duplicate, to notify the Secretary of State that service is being effected pursuant to this subsection and to pay the Secretary of State the sum of $50 for the use of the State, which sum shall be taxed as part of the costs in the proceeding, if the plaintiff shall prevail therein. …
-- Gloss: the plaintiff's duties: serve process and any other papers in duplicate, notify the Secretary of State that service is being effected under this subsection, and pay the Secretary of State $50 for the use of the State.
-- Paying $50 or more discharges the duty to "pay the Secretary of State the sum of $50" (Fork register F-390-3).
-- The $50 "shall be taxed as part of the costs in the proceeding, if the plaintiff shall prevail therein"; if the plaintiff does not prevail the text does not say, so NOTHING.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 390(b)(5) (src:2012)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 390(b)(5) the sum that the plaintiff pays the Secretary of State on service` MEANS 50

@ref 8 Del. C. § 390(b)(5) (src:2012)
GIVEN `process and any other papers are served in duplicate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the plaintiff has notified the Secretary of State that service is being effected under this subsection` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sum paid to the Secretary of State, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 390(b)(5) the plaintiff has done what the duty on service requires` `process and any other papers are served in duplicate` `the plaintiff has notified the Secretary of State that service is being effected under this subsection` `the sum paid to the Secretary of State, in dollars` MEANS
        `process and any other papers are served in duplicate`
    AND `the plaintiff has notified the Secretary of State that service is being effected under this subsection`
    AND (`the sum paid to the Secretary of State, in dollars` AT LEAST `s 390(b)(5) the sum that the plaintiff pays the Secretary of State on service`)

@ref 8 Del. C. § 390(b)(5) (src:2012)
GIVEN `the plaintiff prevails in the proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 390(b)(5) the sum paid to the Secretary of State is taxed as part of the costs` `the plaintiff prevails in the proceeding` MEANS
    IF   `the plaintiff prevails in the proceeding`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2012 | The Secretary of State shall maintain an alphabetical record of any such service setting forth the name of the plaintiff and the defendant, the title, docket number and nature of the proceeding in which process has been served, the fact that service has been effected pursuant to this subsection, the return date thereof, and the day and hour service was made. The Secretary of State shall not be required to retain such information longer than 5 years from receipt of the service of process.
-- Gloss: the Secretary of State keeps an alphabetical record of each such service, and "shall not be required to retain such information longer than 5 years from receipt": retained for 5 years, not required after.
-- The record's particulars (plaintiff and defendant, title, docket number and nature of the proceeding, the fact of service, the return date, the day and hour) are the Secretary of State's own record-keeping.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 390(b)(5) (src:2012)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 390(b)(5) the number of years from receipt of the service for which the Secretary of State must retain the record` MEANS 5

@ref 8 Del. C. § 390(b)(5) (src:2012)
GIVEN `the years since receipt of the service of process` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 390(b)(5) the Secretary of State is required to retain the record of the service` `the years since receipt of the service of process` MEANS
    IF   `the years since receipt of the service of process` AT LEAST 0
    THEN JUST (`the years since receipt of the service of process` AT MOST `s 390(b)(5) the number of years from receipt of the service for which the Secretary of State must retain the record`)
    ELSE NOTHING


§ `Section 390(c) - cessation of the corporation's existence in this State`

-- src:2015 | (c) Upon the filing of a certificate of transfer in accordance with subsection (b) of this section and payment to the Secretary of State of all fees prescribed under this title, the Secretary of State shall certify that the corporation has filed all documents and paid all fees required by this title, and thereupon the corporation shall cease to exist as a corporation of this State at the time the certificate of transfer becomes effective in accordance with § 103 of this title. …
-- Gloss: on the filing of a certificate of transfer (existence to cease) and payment of all fees prescribed under this title (for the certificate: `s 391(a)(25)`, $1,000), the Secretary of State certifies, and the corporation ceases to exist as a corporation
-- of this State AT THE TIME the certificate of transfer becomes effective under § 103 (piece dg1), so the time in question is a fact the caller states. A certificate of transfer and domestic continuance does not end the Delaware existence (subsection (e)).
@ref 8 Del. C. § 390(c) (src:2015)
GIVEN `a certificate of transfer, not a certificate of transfer and domestic continuance, was filed in accordance with subsection (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all fees prescribed under this title were paid to the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 390(c) the Secretary of State must certify that the corporation has filed all documents and paid all fees required by this title` `a certificate of transfer, not a certificate of transfer and domestic continuance, was filed in accordance with subsection (b)` `all fees prescribed under this title were paid to the Secretary of State` MEANS
        `a certificate of transfer, not a certificate of transfer and domestic continuance, was filed in accordance with subsection (b)`
    AND `all fees prescribed under this title were paid to the Secretary of State`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 390(c) (src:2015)
GIVEN `a certificate of transfer, not a certificate of transfer and domestic continuance, was filed in accordance with subsection (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all fees prescribed under this title were paid to the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the time in question is at or after the time the certificate of transfer becomes effective in accordance with § 103` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 390(c) the corporation has ceased to exist as a corporation of this State` `a certificate of transfer, not a certificate of transfer and domestic continuance, was filed in accordance with subsection (b)` `all fees prescribed under this title were paid to the Secretary of State` `the time in question is at or after the time the certificate of transfer becomes effective in accordance with § 103` MEANS
        `a certificate of transfer, not a certificate of transfer and domestic continuance, was filed in accordance with subsection (b)`
    AND `all fees prescribed under this title were paid to the Secretary of State`
    AND `the time in question is at or after the time the certificate of transfer becomes effective in accordance with § 103`

-- src:2015 | Such certificate of the Secretary of State shall be prima facie evidence of the transfer, domestication or continuance by such corporation out of this State.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 390(c) (src:2015)
GIVEN `the Secretary of State has issued the certificate that the corporation has filed all documents and paid all fees required by this title` IS A BOOLEAN
