`s 390(c) the certificate of the Secretary of State is prima facie evidence of the transfer, domestication or continuance out of this State` `the Secretary of State has issued the certificate that the corporation has filed all documents and paid all fees required by this title` MEANS
    `the Secretary of State has issued the certificate that the corporation has filed all documents and paid all fees required by this title`

§ `Section 390(d) - what the transfer leaves unaffected; no winding up`

-- src:2016 | (d) The transfer, domestication or continuance of a corporation out of this State in accordance with this section and the resulting cessation of its existence as a corporation of this State pursuant to a certificate of transfer shall not be deemed to affect any obligations or liabilities of the corporation incurred prior to such transfer, domestication or continuance, the personal liability of any person incurred prior to such transfer, domestication or continuance, or the choice of law applicable to the corporation with respect to matters arising prior to such transfer, domestication or continuance. …
-- Gloss: the transfer "shall not be deemed to affect" (i) obligations or liabilities incurred before, (ii) the personal liability of any person incurred before, (iii) the choice of law applicable to the corporation for matters arising before.
-- Anything else is not addressed by this sentence, so NOTHING.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 390(d) (src:2016)
DECLARE `s 390(d) Matter that the transfer leaves unaffected` IS ONE OF
    `an obligation or liability of the corporation incurred prior to the transfer, domestication or continuance`
    `the personal liability of a person incurred prior to the transfer, domestication or continuance`
    `the choice of law applicable to the corporation with respect to matters arising prior to the transfer, domestication or continuance`
    `another matter that the first sentence of s 390(d) does not name`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 390(d) (src:2016)
GIVEN matter IS A `s 390(d) Matter that the transfer leaves unaffected`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 390(d) the transfer, domestication or continuance leaves the matter unaffected` matter MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
    WHEN `another matter that the first sentence of s 390(d) does not name` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:2016 | Unless otherwise agreed or otherwise provided in the certificate of incorporation, the transfer, domestication or continuance of a corporation out of the State of Delaware in accordance with this section shall not require such corporation to wind up its affairs or pay its liabilities and distribute its assets under this title and shall not be deemed to constitute a dissolution of such corporation.
-- Gloss: unless the parties have otherwise agreed or the certificate of incorporation otherwise provides, the transfer does not require winding up and is not deemed a dissolution. The "unless" is read as qualifying both limbs
-- (Fork register F-390-2). If it is displaced, the text does not say what follows, so NOTHING.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 390(d) (src:2016)
GIVEN `it is otherwise agreed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate of incorporation otherwise provides` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
