§ `Section 390(e) and (f) - continuance, and the effect of the transfer`

-- src:2017 | (e) If a corporation files a certificate of transfer and domestic continuance, after the time the certificate of transfer and domestic continuance becomes effective, the corporation shall continue to exist as a corporation of this State, and the law of the State of Delaware, including this title, shall apply to the corporation to the same extent as prior to such time. So long as a corporation continues to exist as a corporation of the State of Delaware following the filing of a certificate of transfer and domestic continuance, the continuing corporation and the resulting entity shall, for all purposes of the laws of the State of Delaware, constitute a single entity formed, incorporated, created or otherwise having come into being, as applicable, and existing under the laws of the State of Delaware and the laws of the foreign jurisdiction.
-- Gloss: if a certificate of transfer and domestic continuance is filed, after it becomes effective the corporation CONTINUES to exist as a corporation of this State, with Delaware law applying as before; and while it does,
-- the continuing corporation and the resulting entity are a SINGLE entity, for all purposes of Delaware law, existing under the laws of Delaware and of the foreign jurisdiction.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 390(e) (src:2017)
GIVEN `a certificate of transfer and domestic continuance was filed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate of transfer and domestic continuance has become effective` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 390(e) the corporation continues to exist as a corporation of this State, with the law of this State applying as before` `a certificate of transfer and domestic continuance was filed` `the certificate of transfer and domestic continuance has become effective` MEANS
        `a certificate of transfer and domestic continuance was filed`
    AND `the certificate of transfer and domestic continuance has become effective`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 390(e) (src:2017)
GIVEN `the corporation continues to exist as a corporation of this State following the filing of a certificate of transfer and domestic continuance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 390(e) the continuing corporation and the resulting entity constitute a single entity` `the corporation continues to exist as a corporation of this State following the filing of a certificate of transfer and domestic continuance` MEANS
    IF   `the corporation continues to exist as a corporation of this State following the filing of a certificate of transfer and domestic continuance`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2018 | (f) When a corporation has transferred, domesticated or continued pursuant to this section, for all purposes of the laws of the State of Delaware, the resulting entity shall be deemed to be the same entity as the transferring, domesticating or continuing corporation and shall constitute a continuation of the existence of such corporation in the form of the resulting entity. When any transfer, domestication or continuance shall have become effective under this section, for all purposes of the laws of the State of Delaware, all of the rights, privileges and powers of the corporation that has transferred, domesticated or continued, and all property, real, personal and mixed, and all debts due to such corporation, as well as all other things and causes of action belonging to such corporation, shall remain vested in the resulting entity (and also in the corporation that has transferred, domesticated or continued, if and for so long as such corporation continues its existence as a corporation of this State) and shall be the property of such resulting entity (and also of the corporation that has transferred, domesticated or continued, if and for so long as such corporation continues its existence as a corporation of this State), and the title to any real property vested by deed or otherwise in such corporation shall not revert or be in any way impaired by reason of this title; but all rights of creditors and all liens upon any property of such corporation shall be preserved unimpaired, and all debts, liabilities and duties of such corporation shall remain attached to the resulting entity (and also to the corporation that has transferred, domesticated or continued, if and for so long as such corporation continues its existence as a corporation of this State), and may be enforced against it to the same extent as if said debts, liabilities and duties had originally been incurred or contracted by it in its capacity as such resulting entity. The rights, privileges, powers and interests in property of the corporation, as well as the debts, liabilities and duties of the corporation, shall not be deemed, as a consequence of the transfer, domestication or continuance, to have been transferred to the resulting entity for any purpose of the laws of the State of Delaware.
-- Gloss: when a transfer, domestication or continuance has become effective, for all purposes of Delaware law: the resulting entity is the SAME entity as the corporation, a continuation of its existence; its rights, property, debts due and causes of action
-- remain vested in the resulting entity (and also in the corporation, for so long as it continues its existence as a corporation of this State); title to real property does not revert or become impaired; creditors' rights and liens are preserved;
-- debts, liabilities and duties remain attached to the resulting entity (and also to the corporation, for so long as it continues) and may be enforced against it as if incurred by it as the resulting entity; and none of this is a "transfer" to the resulting entity.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 390(f) (src:2018)
DECLARE `s 390(f) Who holds or bears after the transfer, domestication or continuance` IS ONE OF
    `the resulting entity alone`
    `the resulting entity and also the corporation, for so long as the corporation continues its existence as a corporation of this State`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 390(f) (src:2018)
GIVEN `the transfer, domestication or continuance has become effective under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 390(f) the resulting entity is deemed to be the same entity as the corporation, a continuation of its existence` `the transfer, domestication or continuance has become effective under this section` MEANS
    IF   `the transfer, domestication or continuance has become effective under this section`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

