§ `Section 390(g), (h) - shares, and the vote of the stockholders`

-- src:2019 | (g) In connection with a transfer, domestication or continuance under this section, shares of stock of the transferring, domesticating or continuing corporation may be exchanged for or converted into cash, property, or shares of stock, rights or securities of, or interests in, the resulting entity or, in addition to or in lieu thereof, may be exchanged for or converted into cash, property, or shares of stock, rights or securities of, or interests in, another corporation or other entity or may be cancelled.
-- Gloss: in connection with the transfer, domestication or continuance, shares of stock of the corporation MAY be exchanged for or converted into cash, property, or shares, rights or securities of, or interests in, the resulting entity,
-- or (in addition or in lieu) another corporation or other entity, or MAY be cancelled. Any other treatment is not addressed, so NOTHING. The holder's side: the shares are subject to this power (a liability).
@ref 8 Del. C. § 390(g) (src:2019)
DECLARE `s 390(g) Treatment of the shares of the corporation` IS ONE OF
    `exchanged for or converted into cash in a transfer, domestication or continuance`
    `exchanged for or converted into property in a transfer, domestication or continuance`
    `exchanged for or converted into shares of stock, rights or securities of, or interests in, the resulting entity in a transfer, domestication or continuance`
    `exchanged for or converted into cash, property, or shares of stock, rights or securities of, or interests in, another corporation or other entity in a transfer, domestication or continuance`
    `cancelled in a transfer, domestication or continuance`
    `treated in a way that s 390(g) does not name`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 390(g) (src:2019)
GIVEN treatment IS A `s 390(g) Treatment of the shares of the corporation`
      `it is in connection with a transfer, domestication or continuance under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 390(g) the shares of the corporation may be so treated` treatment `it is in connection with a transfer, domestication or continuance under this section` MEANS
    IF   `it is in connection with a transfer, domestication or continuance under this section`
    THEN CONSIDER treatment
         WHEN `treated in a way that s 390(g) does not name` THEN NOTHING
         OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2020 | (h) No vote of the stockholders of a corporation shall be necessary to authorize a transfer, domestication or continuance if no shares of the stock of such corporation shall have been issued prior to the adoption by the board of directors of the resolution approving the transfer, domestication or continuance.
-- Gloss: if no shares of the stock had been issued before the board adopted the resolution, no vote of the stockholders is necessary; if shares had been issued, the vote of subsection (b) is. (Fork register F-390-8)
@ref 8 Del. C. § 390(h) (src:2020)
GIVEN `shares of the stock of the corporation have been issued prior to the adoption by the board of directors of the resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 390(h) a vote of the stockholders is necessary to authorize the transfer, domestication or continuance` `shares of the stock of the corporation have been issued prior to the adoption by the board of directors of the resolution` MEANS
    `shares of the stock of the corporation have been issued prior to the adoption by the board of directors of the resolution`

§ `Section 390(i) - nonstock corporations`

-- src:2021 | (i) Whenever it shall be desired to transfer to or domesticate or continue in any foreign jurisdiction any nonstock corporation, the governing body shall perform all the acts necessary to effect a transfer, domestication or continuance which are required by this section to be performed by the board of directors of a corporation having capital stock. …
-- Gloss: for a nonstock corporation (the core's `Kind of corporation`, not `a stock corporation`) the governing body does what the board does.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 390(i) (src:2021)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of corporation`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 390(i) the governing body performs the acts required of the board of directors` kind MEANS
    IF   `the kind is a nonstock corporation` kind
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2021 | If the members of a nonstock corporation are entitled to vote for the election of members of its governing body or are entitled under the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws of such corporation to vote on such transfer, domestication or continuance or on a merger, consolidation, or dissolution of the corporation, they, and any other holder of any membership interest in the corporation, shall perform all the acts necessary to effect a transfer, domestication or continuance which are required by this section to be performed by the stockholders of a corporation having capital stock. If there is no member entitled to vote thereon, nor any other holder of any membership interest in the corporation, the transfer, domestication or continuance of the corporation shall be authorized at a meeting of the governing body, upon the adoption of a resolution to transfer or domesticate or continue by the vote of a majority of members of its governing body then in office. …
-- Gloss: (A) if the members are entitled to vote for the election of members of the governing body, or are entitled under the certificate or bylaws to vote on this transfer or on a merger, consolidation or dissolution, THEY and any other holder of a
-- membership interest do what the stockholders do; (B) if no member is entitled to vote on it AND there is no other holder of any membership interest, the governing body authorizes it at a meeting by a majority of its members then in office.
-- Any other mix (for example a holder of a membership interest but no member entitled to vote) is not addressed, so NOTHING.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 390(i) (src:2021)
DECLARE `s 390(i) Who authorizes the transfer, domestication or continuance of a nonstock corporation` IS ONE OF
    `the members entitled to vote, and any other holder of a membership interest`
    `the governing body at a meeting, by a majority of its members then in office`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 390(i) (src:2021)
GIVEN `the members are entitled to vote for the election of members of the governing body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the members are entitled under the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws to vote on this transfer, domestication or continuance or on a merger, consolidation or dissolution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any member is entitled to vote on this transfer, domestication or continuance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is another holder of a membership interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 390(i) Who authorizes the transfer, domestication or continuance of a nonstock corporation`
`s 390(i) who authorizes the transfer, domestication or continuance of a nonstock corporation` `the members are entitled to vote for the election of members of the governing body` `the members are entitled under the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws to vote on this transfer, domestication or continuance or on a merger, consolidation or dissolution` `any member is entitled to vote on this transfer, domestication or continuance` `there is another holder of a membership interest` MEANS
    IF   `the members are entitled to vote for the election of members of the governing body`
         OR `the members are entitled under the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws to vote on this transfer, domestication or continuance or on a merger, consolidation or dissolution`
    THEN JUST `the members entitled to vote, and any other holder of a membership interest`
    ELSE IF   (NOT `any member is entitled to vote on this transfer, domestication or continuance`) AND (NOT `there is another holder of a membership interest`)
         THEN JUST `the governing body at a meeting, by a majority of its members then in office`
         ELSE NOTHING

@ref 8 Del. C. § 390(i) (src:2021)
GIVEN `the votes of the members of the governing body in favor of the resolution` IS A NUMBER
      `the members of the governing body then in office` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 390(i) the governing body has authorized the transfer, domestication or continuance by the vote of a majority of its members then in office` `the votes of the members of the governing body in favor of the resolution` `the members of the governing body then in office` MEANS
    `the vote carries` (`a majority of` `the directors then in office`) `the votes of the members of the governing body in favor of the resolution` `the members of the governing body then in office`

-- src:2021 | In all other respects, the method and proceedings for the transfer, domestication or continuance of a nonstock corporation shall conform as nearly as may be to the proceedings prescribed by this section for the transfer, domestication or continuance of corporations having capital stock. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 390(i) (src:2021)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of corporation`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 390(i) the method and proceedings conform as nearly as may be to those prescribed by this section for corporations having capital stock` kind MEANS
    IF   `the kind is a nonstock corporation` kind
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2021 | In the case of a charitable nonstock corporation, due notice of the corporation’s intent to effect a transfer, domestication or continuance shall be mailed to the Attorney General of the State of Delaware 10 days prior to the date of the proposed transfer, domestication or continuance.
-- Gloss: only a charitable nonstock corporation (the core's `a charitable nonstock corporation`) must mail due notice to the Attorney General of the State of Delaware, 10 days prior to the date of the proposed transfer, domestication or continuance;
-- mailed exactly 10 days before is in time (Fork register F-390-1). The Attorney General is an official: no seat; the notice is what the corporation owes.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 390(i) (src:2021)
GIVETH A Period
`s 390(i) the least notice to the Attorney General before the proposed transfer, domestication or continuance` MEANS `period in days` 10

@ref 8 Del. C. § 390(i) (src:2021)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of corporation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 390(i) due notice must be mailed to the Attorney General` kind MEANS
    `the kind is a charitable nonstock corporation` kind

@ref 8 Del. C. § 390(i) (src:2021)
GIVEN `the date on which the notice was mailed to the Attorney General` IS A DATE
      `the date of the proposed transfer, domestication or continuance` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 390(i) the notice to the Attorney General was mailed in time` `the date on which the notice was mailed to the Attorney General` `the date of the proposed transfer, domestication or continuance` MEANS
    `the date on which the notice was mailed to the Attorney General` AT MOST (`the date` `s 390(i) the least notice to the Attorney General before the proposed transfer, domestication or continuance` `before` `the date of the proposed transfer, domestication or continuance`)

§ `Section 390(j) - the plan of transfer, domestication or continuance`

-- src:2022 | (j) In connection with a transfer, domestication or continuance under this section, the transferring, domesticating or continuing corporation may adopt a plan of transfer, domestication or continuance, as applicable, that may state: (i) the terms and conditions of the transfer, domestication or continuance, (ii) the mode of carrying the same into effect, (iii) that the document, instrument, agreement or other writing, as the case may be, governing the internal affairs of the resulting entity and the conduct of its business shall be as set forth in an attachment to the plan, (iv) the manner, if any, of exchanging or converting shares of stock of the corporation of this State which are to be expected for or converted into cash, property, or shares of stock, rights or securities of, or interests in, the resulting entity or, in addition to or in lieu thereof, cash, property, shares of stock, rights or securities of, or interests in, another domestic corporation or other entity or cancelling such shares, in accordance with subsection (g) of this section, (v) any details or provisions as are deemed desirable, and (vi) such other provisions or facts as shall be required to be set forth in a plan of transfer, domestication or continuance, as applicable, by the laws applicable to the resulting entity. …
-- Gloss: the corporation may adopt a plan, which may state any of (i) to (vi). The corporation's side: the power; no other party is bound by it until it is approved (subsection (b)).
-- Note: item (iv) as deposited reads "shares of stock of the corporation of this State which are to be expected for or converted into cash, property ...". "Expected" is read as "exchanged"
-- (subsection (g) says "may be exchanged for or converted into"); the text is not altered and the reading is recorded (Fork register F-390-4).
@ref 8 Del. C. § 390(j) (src:2022)
DECLARE `s 390(j) Statement that a plan of transfer, domestication or continuance may make` IS ONE OF
    `the terms and conditions of the transfer, domestication or continuance`
    `the mode of carrying the same into effect`
    `that the governing document of the resulting entity shall be as set forth in an attachment to the plan`
    `the manner, if any, of exchanging or converting shares of stock of the corporation or cancelling them, in accordance with subsection (g)`
    `any details or provisions as are deemed desirable`
    `such other provisions or facts as shall be required by the laws applicable to the resulting entity`
    `a statement that s 390(j) does not list`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 390(j) (src:2022)
GIVEN statement IS A `s 390(j) Statement that a plan of transfer, domestication or continuance may make`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 390(j) the plan may state it` statement MEANS
    CONSIDER statement
    WHEN `a statement that s 390(j) does not list` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:2022 | Any of the terms of the plan of transfer, domestication or continuance may be made dependent upon facts ascertainable outside of such plan, provided that the manner in which such facts shall operate upon the terms of the plan is clearly and expressly set forth in the plan. …
-- Gloss: a term may depend on facts outside the plan only if the manner in which those facts operate on the terms is clearly and expressly set forth in the plan.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 390(j) (src:2022)
GIVEN `the manner in which the facts operate upon the terms of the plan is clearly and expressly set forth in the plan` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 390(j) a term of the plan may be made dependent upon facts ascertainable outside of the plan` `the manner in which the facts operate upon the terms of the plan is clearly and expressly set forth in the plan` MEANS
    `the manner in which the facts operate upon the terms of the plan is clearly and expressly set forth in the plan`

-- src:2022 | The term “facts,” as used in the preceding sentence, includes, but is not limited to, the occurrence of any event, including a determination or action by any person or body, including the resulting entity or the transferring, domesticating or continuing corporation.
-- Gloss: in the preceding sentence "facts" includes, but is not limited to, the occurrence of any event, and a determination or action by any person or body, including the resulting entity or the transferring, domesticating or continuing corporation.
-- The list is "not limited to", so a fact of another kind is not shown NOT to be one: NOTHING (not covered). (Fork register F-390-5)
@ref 8 Del. C. § 390(j) (src:2022)
DECLARE `s 390(j) Kind of fact on which a term of the plan may depend` IS ONE OF
    `the occurrence of any event`
    `a determination or action by any person or body, including the resulting entity or the transferring, domesticating or continuing corporation`
    `a fact of another kind that s 390(j) does not name`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 390(j) (src:2022)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 390(j) Kind of fact on which a term of the plan may depend`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 390(j) the fact is a fact within the meaning of the preceding sentence` kind MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `a fact of another kind that s 390(j) does not name` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 390(k) - restrictions on mergers and consolidations`

-- src:2023 | (k) Any provision of the certificate of incorporation of a corporation incorporated before August 1, 2023, or any provision in any voting trust agreement or other written agreement between or among any such corporation and 1 or more of its stockholders in effect on or before August 1, 2023, that restricts, conditions or prohibits the consummation of a merger or consolidation shall be deemed to apply to a transfer, domestication or continuance as if it were a merger or consolidation unless the certificate of incorporation or such agreement expressly provides otherwise with respect to a transfer, domestication or continuance or, if the certificate of incorporation or such agreement does not so expressly provide, a conversion, in which case such express provision shall be deemed to apply to a transfer, domestication or continuance as if it were a conversion.
-- Gloss: a provision of the certificate of incorporation of a corporation incorporated BEFORE 1 August 2023, or of a voting trust agreement or other written agreement between or among such a corporation and 1 or more of its stockholders IN EFFECT ON OR BEFORE
-- 1 August 2023, that restricts, conditions or prohibits a merger or consolidation, is DEEMED to apply to a transfer, domestication or continuance as if it were a merger or consolidation, UNLESS the certificate or agreement expressly provides otherwise
-- for a transfer, domestication or continuance (then that express provision governs); or, if it does not so provide, expressly provides for a conversion (then that express provision applies to a transfer, domestication or continuance as if it were a conversion). (Fork register F-390-6: the certificate must have been incorporated strictly before 1 August 2023, the agreement in effect on or before it; F-390-7: the order in which the express provisions are looked for.)
@ref 8 Del. C. § 390(k) (src:2023)
GIVETH A DATE
`s 390(k) the date before which the corporation must have been incorporated, and on or before which the agreement must have been in effect` MEANS YMD 2023 8 1

@ref 8 Del. C. § 390(k) (src:2023)
DECLARE `s 390(k) Where the restriction is found` IS ONE OF
    `in the certificate of incorporation of the corporation (s 390(k))`
    `in a voting trust agreement or other written agreement between or among the corporation and 1 or more of its stockholders (s 390(k))`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 390(k) (src:2023)
DECLARE `s 390(k) How the restriction applies to a transfer, domestication or continuance` IS ONE OF
    `as if the transfer, domestication or continuance were a merger or consolidation`
    `as the certificate or agreement expressly provides with respect to a transfer, domestication or continuance`
    `as if the transfer, domestication or continuance were a conversion`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 390(k) (src:2023)
GIVEN `where the restriction is found` IS A `s 390(k) Where the restriction is found`
      `the date on which the corporation was incorporated` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the agreement came into effect` IS A DATE
      `the provision restricts, conditions or prohibits the consummation of a merger or consolidation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate or agreement expressly provides otherwise with respect to a transfer, domestication or continuance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate or agreement expressly provides with respect to a conversion` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 390(k) How the restriction applies to a transfer, domestication or continuance`
`s 390(k) how the restriction applies to a transfer, domestication or continuance` `where the restriction is found` `the date on which the corporation was incorporated` `the date on which the agreement came into effect` `the provision restricts, conditions or prohibits the consummation of a merger or consolidation` `the certificate or agreement expressly provides otherwise with respect to a transfer, domestication or continuance` `the certificate or agreement expressly provides with respect to a conversion` MEANS
    IF   `the provision restricts, conditions or prohibits the consummation of a merger or consolidation`
         AND (CONSIDER `where the restriction is found`
              WHEN `in the certificate of incorporation of the corporation (s 390(k))` THEN `the date on which the corporation was incorporated` LESS THAN `s 390(k) the date before which the corporation must have been incorporated, and on or before which the agreement must have been in effect`
              WHEN `in a voting trust agreement or other written agreement between or among the corporation and 1 or more of its stockholders (s 390(k))` THEN `the date on which the agreement came into effect` AT MOST `s 390(k) the date before which the corporation must have been incorporated, and on or before which the agreement must have been in effect`)
    THEN JUST (IF `the certificate or agreement expressly provides otherwise with respect to a transfer, domestication or continuance`
               THEN `as the certificate or agreement expressly provides with respect to a transfer, domestication or continuance`
               ELSE IF `the certificate or agreement expressly provides with respect to a conversion`
                    THEN `as if the transfer, domestication or continuance were a conversion`
                    ELSE `as if the transfer, domestication or continuance were a merger or consolidation`)
    ELSE NOTHING
